<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Cholula</h1><p class="st-meta">1168 CE – 1521 CE (approx.) · capital Cholula</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A great holy city of the Puebla valley, home to the largest pyramid by volume in the world and a centre of the cult of Quetzalcoatl.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Cholula was inhabited from the Preclassic, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-pyramid-of-cholula">Great Pyramid</a>, Tlachihualtepetl, was built in stages from about 200 BCE. Traditions in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/historia-tolteca-chichimeca">Historia Tolteca-Chichimeca</a> say Tolteca-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichimeca">Chichimeca</a> groups took control of the city in 1168, founding the Postclassic state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Postclassic Cholula was ruled by two high priests and a council of nobles rather than a king. It was a famous pilgrimage centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quetzalcoatl">Quetzalcoatl</a> and a market city, known for fine polychrome pottery. Cholula had shifting alliances with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tlaxcala">Tlaxcala</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/huexotzinco">Huexotzinco</a> and at times with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1519 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a> and his Tlaxcalan allies massacred thousands of Cholulans in the main temple precinct. The Spanish built churches over its shrines, including one atop the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-pyramid-of-cholula">Great Pyramid</a>, and Cholula became a Spanish town.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1168 CE – 1521 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.95%;width:7.02%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1168 CE – 1521 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cholula</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mesoamerican religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Nahuatl</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cholollan, Cholula altepetl</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1344&amp;focus=cholula" aria-label="Cholula on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2021 1471 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cholula lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2341 1727L2321 1717"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2321 1717h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2341 1727h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2341 1727h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cholula. <a href="/atlas?year=1344&amp;focus=cholula">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
